From 69e76694e62fb62e0d8224b8896f2b484c4d2eec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aman <3285444+realav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 14:01:39 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat: add new_window_with_command keybind action
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Upstream has no keybind action that can open a window running a specific
command. `new_window` takes no argument, and while `ghostty +new-window`
does accept `--command`, it is Linux-only: the macOS apprt returns false
for every IPC action.

That leaves `text:`-based workarounds as the only option on macOS, which
only work when a shell is reading the surface — a full-screen TUI simply
swallows the key.

This adds:

    keybind = cmd+escape=new_window_with_command:claude

The command overrides the `command` config for the new window's first
surface only; working directory inheritance and focus behavior match
`new_window`. It resolves inside libghostty's binding layer, so it fires
regardless of what is running in the focused surface.

Implemented additively — no existing type or behavior is modified — to
keep rebases against upstream main quiet.
